3029..3104 Comment "/// Spinning undoes winding at every word: the round trip at a variable, by"
3105..3179 Comment "/// induction over the presented words. The result type reads the word the"
3180..3251 Comment "/// fold descends on, so each arm answers it at its constructor and the"
3252..3310 Comment "/// recursive call at the field: `sectWords[<](x)` relates"
3311..3386 Comment "/// `spinWords(windWords(x))` to `x`, and carried along `around` it relates"
3387..3461 Comment "/// `Loop(spinWords(windWords(x)))`, which `spinWords(windWords(Loop(x)))`"
3462..3539 Comment "/// runs to, to `Loop(x)`. The case respects both rules: at `Loop(Unloop(x))`"
3540..3614 Comment "/// the arms compose to `cong(around, cong(unaround, p))`, whose functions"
3615..3691 Comment "/// compose to the identity under the rules, so the chain is `p` itself, the"
3692..3710 Comment "/// answer at `x`."
